## 15. Backend Authorization Middleware

Create reusable Express.js middleware.

Example architecture:

- authenticateUser()
- authenticateAdmin()
- requirePermission(permission)
- requireRole(role)
- requireMfa()
- validateSession()
- requireActiveAccount()
- rateLimitLogin()
- validateCsrfToken()

Every protected API endpoint must use appropriate middleware.

Never trust:
- User role sent by the browser.
- User ID sent by the browser.
- Permission claims that have not been validated.
- Client-supplied account status.
- Client-supplied administrative privileges.

Identify users from the validated server-side authentication context.

Use server-side database checks or securely managed authorization data to prevent stale privileges from remaining effective after account or permission changes.

