## 22. Mandatory Security Rules

1. Never store plain-text passwords.
2. Never store authentication tokens in localStorage.
3. Never allow public administrator registration.
4. Never trust frontend role or permission information.
5. Never expose database credentials or secrets to React.
6. Never allow unauthorized privilege escalation.
7. Never bypass backend permission middleware.
8. Never allow suspended or deactivated accounts to authenticate.
9. Never log passwords, OTPs, or raw authentication tokens.
10. Never allow unauthorized users to access another user's account.
11. Never delete critical audit history through ordinary application interfaces.
12. Never use fake authentication or hardcoded production credentials.
13. Apply secure password recovery and session invalidation.
14. Protect all privileged operations with appropriate authorization.
15. Require MFA for privileged administrator accounts.
16. Make security-critical changes auditable.

Follow current OWASP Application Security Verification Standard (ASVS) guidance and applicable OWASP security best practices.

